hadiths[94]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1103","Narrated by Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her): The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) married me when I was seven years old, and consummated the marriage with me when I was nine years old. I used to play with dolls, and there were little girls who would come to me. When they saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), they would hide from him, and the Prophet (ﷺ) would send them to me."
"1104","Narrated by Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her): The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) married me when I was six years old, and consummated the marriage with me when I was nine years old."
"1105","Abu Bakr bin Abdur Rahman bin Harith bin Hisham narrates from Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said: When she came to Madinah, she informed the people of Madinah that she was the daughter of Abu Umayyah bin Mughirah, but they did not believe her and said: ""How many lies strangers tell."" Until one of them went for Hajj, and he said: Do you want to write a message for your family? She wrote a message and gave it to him. When he returned to Madinah, he confirmed her identity and began to honor her even more than before. She says: When I became lawful (my waiting period ended), the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to me and proposed marriage to me. I said to him: Who would marry someone like me? I will not have (more) children, and I am jealous and have children. He (ﷺ) said: ""I am older than you, as for jealousy, Allah will remove it, and children are for Allah and His Messenger (ﷺ)."" Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) married her, and when he (ﷺ) would come to her, he would say: ""Where is Zunab?"" Until Ammar bin Yasir (may Allah be pleased with him) came and quickly snatched him (the child) from the lap of Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) and said: He is keeping the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) away, while she (Umm Salamah) was breastfeeding him. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came and said: ""Where is Zunab?"" Qareebah bint Abu Umayyah, who was present at that time, said: Ammar bin Yasir (may Allah be pleased with him) has taken him. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""I will come to you at night."" Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) says: I got up and spread the leather mat that is placed under the millstone, and took out barley grains from the jar, then took out fat and squeezed it over them (prepared a dish). She says: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) spent the night and stayed until morning. When morning came, he (ﷺ) said: ""Indeed, you have honor among your family, if you wish, I will appoint seven days for you, and if I appoint seven days, I will also appoint seven for my other wives."""
"1106","It is narrated from Abdul Malik bin Abu Bakr bin Abdur Rahman that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her), and morning came at her place, he ﷺ said to her: ""Because of you, there will be no disgrace upon your family. If you wish, I will stay with you for seven days, and seven days with them, and if you wish, I will stay with you for three days, then I will assign turns."" Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: ""You may stay for three days."""
"1107","It is narrated from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: For a virgin, there are seven days (for the husband to spend the nights with her after marriage), and in the case of marrying a widow, there are three days."
"1108","It is narrated from Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) proposed to her, then mentioned his marriage and spending the night with her, and also mentioned what he said to Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her): ""If you wish, I will stay with you for seven days, and likewise with them (the other wives) for seven days."""
"1109","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that when the Prophet (ﷺ) passed away, he had nine wives in his marriage, and he had assigned turns for eight of them."
"1110","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) departed from this world while he had nine wives in his marriage, and he had assigned turns for eight of them."
"1111","Hisham narrates from his father that Sawda (may Allah be pleased with her) gave her turn (day) to Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) as a gift."
"1112","It is narrated from the noble wife of the Prophet ﷺ, Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: When the Prophet ﷺ intended to travel, he would draw lots among his wives. Whosever name was drawn, he would take her with him (on the journey)."
"1113","It is narrated from Abu Salamah (may Allah be pleased with him), he says: I asked Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), ""What was the dowry of the Prophet ﷺ (that he gave to his wives)?"" She replied: ""The dowry of the Prophet ﷺ for his wives was twelve uqiyah and one nash."" Then she said: ""Do you know how much a nash is?"" I said: ""No,"" so she said: ""Half an uqiyah."""
"1114","It is narrated from Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) arrived in Madinah, he drew lots for the residences of the people. The lot of Abdur Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) came out in the name of Sa’d bin Rabi’ (may Allah be pleased with him). So Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: “Come, I will divide my wealth with you, and I will leave for you whichever of my two wives you wish (by separating from her), and I will also work for you.” Abdur Rahman (may Allah be pleased with him) replied: “May Allah bless your family and your wealth for you, just show me the way to the market.” He (may Allah be pleased with him) went to the market and earned some wealth, then he sent a proposal to a woman and married her. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: “O Abdur Rahman! For how much dowry did you marry her?” Abdur Rahman (may Allah be pleased with him) said: “For a gold nugget.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Give a wedding feast, even if it is with only one goat.”"
"1115","It is narrated from Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that Abdur Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and there was a yellow mark on his (clothes or body). The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) inquired about it, and he informed him that he had married a woman from among the Ansar. Upon this, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""How much dowry did you give?"" He replied: ""I gave gold equal to the weight of a date stone."" Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to him: ""Give a wedding feast, even if it is with only one goat."""
"1116","It is narrated from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that Abdur Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) married for the amount of gold equal to the weight of a date stone."
"1117","It is narrated from Sahl bin Sa’d Al-Sa’idi (may Allah be pleased with him) that a woman came to the service of the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah! I have gifted myself to you.” She stood for a long time. Then a companion stood up and said: “O Messenger of Allah! Marry her to me if you have no need of her.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Do you have anything to give her as a dowry?” That companion (may Allah be pleased with him) said: “I have nothing except this lower garment.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “If you give her that, you will sit down without a lower garment. Look for something else.” He said: “I find nothing.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Look, even if it is an iron ring.” The companion searched but found nothing. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Do you know anything of the Qur’an by heart?” He said: “Yes, such and such surahs,” and he named the surahs. Upon this, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I have married her to you for the dowry of what you know of the Qur’an (i.e., you will teach her).”"
"1118","It is narrated from Sahl (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) married a woman to a man in exchange for some chapters of the Qur'an."
"1119","It is narrated from Abu Hazim bin Dinar that he heard Sahl bin Sa’d Al-Sa’idi (may Allah be pleased with him) say that a companion sent a proposal of marriage to a woman who was standing near the Prophet (ﷺ). The Prophet (ﷺ) spoke to him about her dowry and said: “Go and look, even if it is only an iron ring.”"
"1120","It is narrated from Ikrimah bin Khalid that the son of Umm Hakim, during his illness, said to his wife that she should give something to him from his inheritance, but the woman refused. So the son of Umm Hakim said, ""I will include in this inheritance those who will diminish your right or prove harmful in it."" Therefore, during his illness, he married three women, and gave each of them a dowry of one thousand. Abdul Malik bin Marwan declared this permissible. Saeed bin Salim says, ""If the dowry of these women is equal to the customary dowry, then it is valid, and if it is more than the customary amount, then the excess should be returned."""
"1121","Ikrimah bin Khalid narrates that Abdur Rahman bin Umm Hakam, during his illness, intended that his wife should take out a share from his inheritance (for charity, etc.), but the woman refused. So he married three other women and gave each of them a dowry of one thousand dinars. Abdul Malik bin Marwan declared it permissible and made all of them partners in the eighth share. Imam Shafi’i (may Allah have mercy on him) said: “In my opinion, this was the mahr al-mithl (customary dowry), and if it is more than the mahr al-mithl, then the marriage is still valid, but the amount exceeding the mahr al-mithl will be invalid if he dies in that same illness. Because this is in the ruling of a bequest, and a bequest is not permissible for an heir.”"
"1122","Nafi’, the freed slave of Ibn ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with them), narrated that the daughter of Hafs bin Mughira was married to ‘Abdullah bin Abi Rabiah, and he divorced her. Then ‘Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) married her. It was reported to him that this woman was barren and did not bear children, so he divorced her before consummating the marriage. She remained in this state during the life of ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) and for some time during the caliphate of ‘Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him). Then ‘Abdullah bin Abi Rabiah married her again while he was ill, so that she could inherit from him among his wives, and there was also kinship between them."
"1123","It is narrated from Nafi' (may Allah have mercy on him) that Ibn Abi Rabiah contracted marriage during illness and it was considered permissible."
"1124","It is narrated from Amr bin Dinar that Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) intended not to marry, so Hafsa (may Allah be pleased with her) said to him, ""Get married; if you have children, they will pray for you after you have passed away."""
"1125","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""None of you should send a marriage proposal over the proposal of his brother."""
"1126","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) similar to the previous hadith. And some hadith scholars have added these words: ""until he seeks permission from him or he breaks off the engagement."""
"1127","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should propose to a woman to whom his brother has already proposed."""
"1128","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that he stated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should propose marriage over the proposal of his brother."""
"1129","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Prophet (ﷺ) forbade a man from proposing to a woman to whom his brother has already proposed, until he marries her or leaves her (i.e., breaks off the engagement)."
"1130","Abdur Rahman bin Qasim narrates from his father that regarding the command of Allah Almighty: ""There is no sin upon you if you hint at a proposal of marriage to women"" (Al-Baqarah: 235), he says: Its meaning is that a man may say to a woman during her waiting period after her husband's death: ""You are honorable to me, I am inclined towards you, Allah Almighty will bring goodness or sustenance to you,"" or he may say something similar to this."
"1131","It is narrated from Fatimah bint Qais (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to her: ""When your waiting period ('iddah) is over, inform me."" She says: When my 'iddah was over, I informed the Prophet (ﷺ) that Muawiyah and Abu Jahm (may Allah be pleased with them both) had proposed marriage to me. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Muawiyah is a poor man, he has no wealth, and as for Abu Jahm, he never puts his stick down from his shoulder (i.e., he beats women). Marry Usamah bin Zaid."" So I married him, and Allah placed so much goodness and blessing in that marriage that other women began to envy me."
"1132","Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her) bint Qais narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to her, in the case of divorce from her husband during her waiting period: ""When your waiting period is complete, inform me."" She says: When my waiting period was complete, I informed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that Muawiyah and Abu Jahm (may Allah be pleased with them both) had sent me proposals of marriage. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Muawiyah is a poor man, he has no wealth, and as for Abu Jahm, he does not put his stick down from his shoulder (i.e., he beats women), so marry Usamah."" She says: I disliked this suggestion, but the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said again: ""Marry Usamah (may Allah be pleased with him)."" So I married him, and Allah put so much goodness in it that women began to envy me."
"1133","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that he said: A marriage does not take place without a guardian, a wali, and two trustworthy witnesses."
"1134","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that he stated: A marriage does not take place without a guardian, two trustworthy witnesses, and a guiding guardian, and in my opinion, Muslim heard this from Ibn Khuthaym."
"1135","It is narrated from one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ that the Prophet ﷺ said: ""When two guardians perform a marriage, the marriage of the one who did it first is valid, and when two authorized persons sell the same thing, the sale of the one who sold it first will be valid."""
"1136","It is narrated from Uqbah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When two guardians arrange a marriage, the marriage of the first is valid."""
"1137","Abdur Rahman bin Qasim narrated from his father, who said: When a marriage proposal (khitbah) was made for a woman from the family of Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) and she was present, when only the marriage contract (nikah) remained, she would say to one of the men from the household: ""Marry her off,"" because a woman cannot be the guardian (wali) in the marriage contract."
"1138","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: ""No woman should act as a guardian to marry off another woman; indeed, an immoral woman marries herself off."""
"1139","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates from the Prophet ﷺ that he ﷺ said: ""Any woman who marries without the permission of her guardian, her marriage is invalid."" He ﷺ repeated these words three times."
"1140","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates from the Prophet (ﷺ) that he said: ""Any woman who marries without the permission of her guardian, her marriage is invalid. If the man has intercourse with her, he must pay the dowry, because he has made her private parts lawful in exchange for it. If the guardians disagree among themselves, then the ruler is the guardian of the one who has no guardian."""
"1141","Amr bin Dinar (may Allah have mercy on him) says that a woman from Banu Bakr bin Kinanah, who was called Bint Abi Thamamah, married Umar bin Abdullah bin Mudarris. Alqamah bin Alqamah Al-Atwari wrote a letter to Umar bin Abdul Aziz (may Allah have mercy on him) (while he was the governor of Madinah) saying: I am the guardian (wali) of this woman and she married without consulting me. Umar annulled this marriage, even though the man had already consummated the marriage with her. He said: Any woman who marries without the permission of her guardian, her marriage is invalid, because the Prophet ﷺ said: ""Her marriage is invalid."" And if the man has consummated the marriage with her, then she is entitled to a mahr equal to that of women of her status, in exchange for what he has taken from her, according to the decision of the Prophet ﷺ regarding such a woman."
"1142","Ikrimah bin Khalid narrated that during a journey, a caravan gathered together and among them was a widow. She appointed one of the men as her guardian, and he married her to another man. So Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) flogged both the one who married and the one who conducted the marriage, and annulled the marriage."
"1143","It is narrated from Abdur Rahman bin Ma’bad that Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) declared the marriage of a woman who married without a guardian to be invalid."
"1144","Abu al-Zubair narrated that a case of marriage was brought to Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) in which there was only one man and one woman as witnesses. So he (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""This is a secret marriage, and I do not consider it permissible, and if I had declared this earlier, I would have stoned (the parties involved)."""
"1145","It is narrated from Umrah bint Abdur Rahman that the Prophet ﷺ cursed both the one who reveals the secrets of seclusion and the one with whom it is done."
"1146","Asma (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated that a woman came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: ""O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)! My daughter had measles and her hair fell out, can I attach artificial hair to her head?"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) replied: ""A curse has been placed upon both the one who attaches artificial hair and the one who has it attached."""
"1147","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""A widow has more right over herself than her guardian, and a virgin should be asked for permission regarding her marriage, and her permission is her silence."""
"1148","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""A widow has more right over herself than her guardian, and a virgin should be asked for permission regarding her marriage, and her silence is her permission."""
"1149","It is narrated from Ibn Jurayj that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered Na'im to consult the girl's mother in the case of her daughter's marriage."
"1150","It is narrated from Khansa bint Khizam (may Allah be pleased with her) that her father married her off while she was previously married (i.e., not a virgin), and she did not approve of this marriage. Therefore, she presented herself before the Prophet ﷺ, and he ﷺ annulled (invalidated) this marriage."
"1151","It is narrated from Sa'id bin al-Musayyib (may Allah have mercy on him) regarding the interpretation of Allah's statement: ""A fornicator does not marry except a fornicatress"" (__QUR_N__: al-Nur: 3), he said: This verse is abrogated, and it has been abrogated by (Allah's command): ""And marry those among you who are single"" (__QUR_N__: al-Nur: 32), and these are the unmarried men and women among the Muslims."
"1152","It is narrated from Sa'id bin al-Musayyib, may Allah have mercy on him, that he said: This is abrogated, and it has been abrogated by (the verse) ""And marry those among you who are single..."" and by this is meant the unmarried men and women among the Muslims, that is, the statement of Allah ""The adulterer does not marry except an adulteress"" is abrogated."
"1153","Abdullah bin Abi Yazid narrated from some people of knowledge that they said about this verse: ""This is decisive between the two."""
"1154","It is narrated from Mujahid (may Allah have mercy on him) that this verse ﴿The adulterer does not marry...﴾ (An-Nur: 4) was revealed about those adulterous women of the Age of Ignorance who used to erect flags on their houses and commit immorality."
"1155","Qais bin Abi Hazim narrated that I heard Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) say: ""We used to fight in jihad with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and we did not have our wives with us, so we intended to become castrated. But the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade us from that, then he permitted us to marry women for a specified period in exchange for something (a dowry)."""
"1156","It is narrated from Qais bin Abi Hazim: I heard Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) say: ""We used to go for jihad with the Prophet (ﷺ) and our wives were not with us. We wanted to become eunuchs, but we were forbidden from doing so. Then we were granted permission to contract marriage with a woman for a specified period in exchange for something."""
"1157","Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said to Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): ""Indeed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade temporary marriage (Nikah Mut'ah) and eating the meat of domestic donkeys."""
"1158","It is narrated from Urwah that Khawlah bint Hakim came to Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) and said, ""Indeed, Rabee’ah bin Umayyah benefited from a woman born among the Arabs, and that woman became pregnant from him."" Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) went out, dragging his cloak in distress, and said: ""This is Mut’ah. If I had already made a statement about it, I would have stoned him."""
"1159","It is narrated from Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) that on the day of Khaybar, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade temporary marriage with women and eating the meat of domestic donkeys."
"1160","Rabi' bin Sabrah narrates from his father that the Prophet ﷺ forbade Nikah Mut'ah."
"1161","It is narrated from Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (ﷺ) forbade temporary marriage (mut'ah) and the eating of domestic donkey meat in the year of Khaybar."
"1162","Rabee’ bin Sabrah narrates from his father that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade Nikah Mut’ah."
"1163","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade Shighar marriage, and Shighar is that a man marries his daughter to another on the condition that he will marry his daughter to him, and there will be no dowry between them."
"1164","Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (ﷺ) forbade Shighar marriage."
"1165","It is narrated from Mujahid that the Prophet ﷺ said: ""There is no shighar in Islam."""
"1166","It is narrated from Ibn Umar and Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Prophet ﷺ forbade shighar. Imam Malik (may Allah have mercy on him) added these words in his narration: Shighar is when a man marries off his daughter to another man on the condition that the latter marries his own daughter to him."
"1167","Qabeesah bin Dhuwaib narrates that a man asked Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) about two sisters who are owned by one man; can he have intercourse with both of them? Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) replied: ""One verse has made both of them lawful, while another verse has made both of them unlawful, and as for myself, I do not like to do this."" Qabeesah said that the man left from him and met one of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, who said: ""If I had any authority in the matter, and then I found a man who had done this, I would make him an example."" Imam Malik (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Ibn Shihab said, ""In my opinion, he is Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him)."" Imam Malik (may Allah have mercy on him) said: ""I have also received similar information regarding Zubair bin Al-Awwam (may Allah be pleased with him)."""
"1168","It is narrated from Ubaidullah bin Utbah that Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked about a woman and her daughter who are both slave girls of the same man: Can a man have intercourse with one of them and then with the other? Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) replied: ""I do not like to declare it permissible to have intercourse with both of them at the same time."""
"1169","Abdullah bin Utbah narrated that Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked about a mother and her daughter who were both owned by the same man, so he said: ""I do not like that we should permit both of them."" Ubaidullah said that my father said, I wish that Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) had been even stricter in this matter."
"1170","Ibn Abi Mulaika narrates that Mu'adh bin Abdullah bin Ubaidullah bin Ma'mar came to Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) and said to her: ""I have a slave woman with whom I have relations, and her daughter is also my slave woman. So can I have relations with her daughter as well?"" Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) replied: ""No."" He said: ""I will not leave her until you say that Allah Almighty has declared this forbidden."" Upon this, Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: ""Neither will anyone from my household do such a thing, nor anyone who follows my words."""
"1171","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man should not combine a woman in marriage with her paternal aunt or her maternal aunt."""
"1172","Umm Habibah bint Abu Sufyan (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: She said, ""O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! Are you interested in my sister, the daughter of Abu Sufyan?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied, ""What would I do?"" Umm Habibah (may Allah be pleased with her) said, ""You should marry her."" He ﷺ said, ""Your sister?"" She said, ""Yes."" He ﷺ said, ""Would you like that?"" (that your sister would be your co-wife) She said, ""Yes, I am not alone with you, and I would like to share goodness and blessing with my sister."" He ﷺ said, ""That is not lawful for me."" Umm Habibah (may Allah be pleased with her) says, I said, ""By Allah! I have been informed that you are going to marry the daughter of Abu Salamah."" He ﷺ said, ""The daughter of Abu Salamah?"" She said, ""Yes."" He ﷺ said, ""By Allah! Even if she were not my stepdaughter and under my guardianship, she would still not be lawful for me, because she is the daughter of my foster brother. Both her father and I were suckled by Thuwaybah. Therefore, do not offer your daughters and sisters to me for marriage."""
"1173","Narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The relationship that becomes unlawful through lineage also becomes unlawful through breastfeeding."""
"1174","It is narrated from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: ""O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)! Do you have any desire for your uncle Hamza's (may Allah be pleased with him) daughter? She is the most beautiful young girl of the Quraysh."" The Prophet (ﷺ) replied: ""Do you not know that Hamza (may Allah be pleased with him) is also my foster brother, and Allah Almighty has made unlawful by reason of suckling those relationships which He has made unlawful by reason of lineage."""
"1175","From another chain through Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), a narration similar to Sufyan's hadith regarding the daughter of Hamza (may Allah be pleased with him) is reported from the Prophet (ﷺ)."
"1176","It is narrated from Amr bin Shuraid that Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) was asked: ""A man has two wives. One of them breastfed a boy belonging to someone, and the other breastfed a girl belonging to someone else. Is the marriage between that boy and girl permissible?"" He replied: ""No. Because the man who provided the semen (from whom the milk of both women was produced) is the same."""
"1177","It is narrated from Umrah bint Abdul Rahman that the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), told her that the Prophet ﷺ was sitting with her when she heard the voice of a man who was seeking permission from Hafsa (may Allah be pleased with her). Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: ""O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! This man is asking permission to enter your house."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""I think this is so-and-so"" (he mentioned the name of Hafsa's foster uncle). So I asked: ""If so-and-so, who was her foster uncle, were alive, could he come to me?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Yes, just as blood relations make something unlawful (for marriage), so does suckling (breastfeeding) establish prohibition."""
"1178","Narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: ""My (foster) uncle Aflih came,"" and she narrated a long hadith."
"1179","It is narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said: ""It was revealed in the Qur'an that ten times suckling makes (marriage) unlawful, then it was abrogated and five times suckling became the cause of prohibition, and only those who had completed five sucklings would come to Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her)."""
"1180","It is narrated from Umm al-Mu'mineen Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said: ""It was revealed in the Qur'an that ten times suckling establishes prohibition (of marriage), then this was abrogated and (the command came) that five times suckling establishes prohibition. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) passed away, this was among the verses that were recited in the Qur'an."""
"1181","It is narrated from Safiyyah bint Abi Ubaid that she informed Nafi‘ that Umm al-Mu’minin Sayyidah Hafsah (may Allah be pleased with her) sent ‘Asim bin ‘Abdullah bin Sa‘d to her sister Fatimah bint ‘Umar to be breastfed ten times so that he could later come to her, and at that time he was a small nursing child. So Fatimah did so, and afterwards he used to come and go to her."
"1182","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Suckling once or twice does not establish prohibition, nor does drinking milk once or twice establish prohibition."""
"1183","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Prohibition is not established by suckling once or twice."""
"1184","Salim bin Abdullah (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated that when he was a nursing infant, Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) sent him to her sister Umm Kulthum, who nursed him three times, then she became ill and could not nurse him more than three times. Therefore, I could not come to Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) because Umm Kulthum had not completed ten nursings for me."
"1185","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: ""Prohibition through suckling does not occur until it fills the intestines (i.e., until the stomach is filled)."""
"1186","It is narrated from Ubaid bin Abdullah bin Zam‘ah that his mother, Zainab bint Abi Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her), was breastfed by Asma bint Abi Bakr (may Allah be pleased with her), the wife of Zubair bin Al-Awwam (may Allah be pleased with him). Zainab bint Abi Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) would come to me while I was combing my hair, and he would take hold of one of my braids and say, “Come, talk to me,” and I considered him my (foster) father and his sons as my brothers. Then, before the incident of Harrah, Abdullah bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with them both) sent a marriage proposal for my daughter Umm Kulthum to Hamzah bin Zubair. Hamzah was from another wife (Kalbiyyah). Zainab said to the messenger of Ibn Zubair (may Allah be pleased with them both): “Is it permissible for her to marry him? For she is his niece.” Then Abdullah bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with them both) again sent a messenger to me and said: “Hamzah is not your brother, for only those sons of Asma (may Allah be pleased with her) are your brothers, and those sons of Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) from women other than Asma are not your brothers. Send someone to investigate this matter.” Zainab says: I sent messengers and also asked myself; at that time, many Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) and Mothers of the Believers were present. All of them told Zainab that nothing becomes unlawful (haram) from the man’s side through breastfeeding. Then Zainab married her daughter (Umm Kulthum) to Hamzah bin Zubair, and she remained in his marriage until his death."
"1187","It is narrated from Ata bin Yasar (may Allah have mercy on him) that breastfeeding on behalf of a man does not make anything unlawful."
"1188","It is narrated from Urwah bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Prophet (ﷺ) instructed Sahla bint Suhail (may Allah be pleased with her) to breastfeed Salim five times so that he would become her mahram."
"1189","It is narrated from Urwah that the Prophet ﷺ instructed the wife of Abu Hudhaifah (Sahlah) to breastfeed Salim five times, and he would become her mahram through her milk. She did so, and she considered Salim as her son."
"1190","Urwah bin Zubair (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated that Abu Hudhaifah bin Utbah bin Rabi’ah (may Allah be pleased with him) was among the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, and he participated in the Battle of Badr. He had adopted Salim as his son, who was called “Salim, the freed slave of Abu Hudhaifah.” Just as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had adopted Zaid bin Harithah (may Allah be pleased with him) as a son. Since Abu Hudhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) considered Salim his son, he married him to his niece Fatimah bint Walid bin Utbah, who was among the first to migrate and at that time was one of the most distinguished unmarried women of the Quraysh. Then, when Allah the Exalted revealed in the Qur’an regarding Zaid bin Harithah (may Allah be pleased with him): “Call them by (the names of) their (real) fathers; that is more just in the sight of Allah. But if you do not know their fathers, then they are your brothers in religion” (Al-Ahzab: 5), everyone returned their adopted sons to their real fathers. Whoever’s father was not known was attributed to their emancipators. After this, Abu Hudhaifah’s (may Allah be pleased with him) wife, Sahla bint Suhail (may Allah be pleased with her), who was from the Banu Amir bin Lu’ayy tribe, came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! We used to consider Salim as our son, and he comes and goes to me while I am in simple home clothing, and our house is one. What do you say about him?” The Prophet ﷺ said: “The ruling regarding what has reached us is that you should give him five breastfeedings, and he will become unlawful for you (as a foster son) through that milk.” She did so, and she considered Salim her foster son. Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) deduced from this that if she wished for a man to be able to come to her, she would order her sister Umm Kulthum and her nieces to breastfeed him (even in adulthood), and then he would come and go to her. All the other wives of the Prophet ﷺ rejected this, saying: “In our opinion, the ruling that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave to Sahla bint Suhail was a special concession only for Salim (may Allah be pleased with him). No one can come to us through such breastfeeding.” This is the matter in which there was a difference among the wives of the Prophet ﷺ regarding the breastfeeding of an adult."
"1191","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that when Ghaylan bin Salamah Thaqafi (may Allah be pleased with him) accepted Islam, he had ten wives. The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him: ""Keep four of them (in marriage) and separate from the rest."""
"1192","The hadith of Ghaylan is also narrated from Imam Malik, may Allah have mercy on him, through the chain of Zuhri."
"1193","Nawfal bin Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that I became Muslim while I had five wives. I asked the Prophet ﷺ, and he ﷺ said: ""Divorce one and keep the remaining four (in marriage)."" So I divorced the first of them, who had been barren for sixty years."
"1194","It is narrated from Dailami or Ibn Dailami (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: ""I embraced Islam and I had two real sisters in my marriage. I asked the Prophet (ﷺ), so he (ﷺ) instructed me to choose whichever one I wished from them and release the other."""
"1195","It is narrated from Ibn Shihab (may Allah have mercy on him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to the man from the tribe of Thaqif who had accepted Islam and had ten wives: ""Keep four and separate (divorce) the rest."""
"1196","It is narrated from Ibn Shihab that Safwan bin Umayyah (may Allah be pleased with him) fled at the time of the conquest of Makkah, then came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and participated in the battles of Hunayn and Ta’if while still in a state of disbelief, whereas his wife had already embraced Islam. The Prophet ﷺ kept them both upon their (previous) marriage. Ibn Shihab said: There was approximately a one-month gap between the Islam of Safwan and his wife."
